{"name":"Thames Dusk","hex":"#62676a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to darkness or blackness; moderately dark or black; dusky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time after the sun has set but when the sky is still lit by sunlight; the evening twilight period.","A darkish colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusk"}],"entries":[{"title":"River Thames","blocks":[{"text":"The River Thames, or simply the Thames, known alternatively in parts as the River Isis, is a river that flows through southern England including London. At 215 miles (346 km), it is the longest river entirely in England and the second-longest in the United Kingdom, after the River Severn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/London_Thames_Sunset_panorama_-_Feb_2008.jpg/330px-London_Thames_Sunset_panorama_-_Feb_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_Thames"},{"title":"Dusk","blocks":[{"text":"Dusk occurs at the darkest stage of twilight, or at the very end of astronomical twilight after sunset and just before nightfall. At predusk, during early to intermediate stages of twilight, enough light in the sky under clear conditions may occur to read outdoors without artificial illumination; however, at the end of civil twilight, such lighting is required to read outside. The term dusk usually refers to astronomical dusk, or the darkest part of twilight before night begins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg/330px-Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusk"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Le_Pilier_des_Nautes_01.JPG/500px-Le_Pilier_des_Nautes_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Le_Pilier_des_Nautes_01.JPG/500px-Le_Pilier_des_Nautes_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Image of the deity Æsus on the Gallo-Roman \"Pillar of the Boatmen\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALe_Pilier_des_Nautes_01.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Father_Thames%2C_St_John%27s_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg/500px-Father_Thames%2C_St_John%27s_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Father_Thames%2C_St_John%27s_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg/1280px-Father_Thames%2C_St_John%27s_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Father_Thames%2C_St_John%27s_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg/500px-Father_Thames%2C_St_John%27s_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A statue of Old Father Thames by Raffaelle Monti at St John's Lock, Lechlade","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFather_Thames%2C_St_John's_Lock%2C_Lechlade.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Thames_by_Anne_Seymour_Damer.JPG/500px-Thames_by_Anne_Seymour_Damer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Thames_by_Anne_Seymour_Damer.JPG/1280px-Thames_by_Anne_Seymour_Damer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Thames_by_Anne_Seymour_Damer.JPG/500px-Thames_by_Anne_Seymour_Damer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikip